Q: Class decorator with arguments using the @decorator syntax not working A: <p>I believe</p>
<pre><code>@decorator_class(&quot;arg&quot;, key=&quot;value&quot;) # &lt;- this is not working
</code></pre>
<p>is not equal to</p>
<pre><code>f = decorator_class(f, &quot;decorator arg&quot;, decorator_kwarg=&quot;value&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>but to</p>
<pre><code>f = decorator_class(&quot;decorator arg&quot;, decorator_kwarg=&quot;value&quot;)(f)
</code></pre>
<p>So to make it work, you need to get an added layer there:</p>
<pre><code>import functools

class decorator_class:
    def __init__(self, *dargs, **dkwargs):
        self.args0 = dargs
        self.kwargs0 = dkwargs

    def __call__(self, func):
        @functools.wraps(func)
        def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):
            print(func.__name__, self.args0, self.kwargs0, args, kwargs)
            return func(*args, **kwargs)
        return wrapper


@decorator_class(&quot;arg&quot;, key=&quot;value&quot;)
def f(*args, **kwargs):
    print(&quot;f&quot;, args, kwargs)

f(&quot;some_arg&quot;, some_kwarg=&quot;some_value&quot;)
</code></pre>

Q: useEffect cleanup runs before mount on prod build only, works fine in dev — React 18.3, Node 20 A: <p>That cannot happen for the same effect instance.</p>
<p>React cannot call the cleanup before running the effect body, because the cleanup function only exists after this code has executed:</p>
<pre><code>useEffect(() =&gt; {
  console.log('mount');
  return () =&gt; console.log('cleanup');
}, []);
</code></pre>
<p>So <code>cleanup -&gt; mount</code> almost certainly comes from two different component instances: an old one unmounting and a new one mounting. Production routing/key changes can make that easier to observe.</p>
<p>Add an instance ID:</p>
<pre><code>const id = useRef(Math.random());

useEffect(() =&gt; {
  console.log('mount', id.current);
  return () =&gt; console.log('cleanup', id.current);
}, []);
</code></pre>
<p>If the IDs differ, that confirms it.</p>
